      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 873718704,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "You mean \"*Prevent* null dereference in `rescan_file()`\", not \"*Recover from*\", as your code doesn't catch a `SIGSEGV` signal on UN*Xes or the equivalent exception on Windows, fix things up, and continue, it adds a null-pointer check.\n\nI.e.,\n\n> It should never happen, but it shouldn't segfault when it does.\n\nmeans \"it should never be the case that `fdata` is null, but it shouldn't crash when it is\".\n\n> Partial fix for #17989 \n\nIf it truly \"should never be the case\", this is a workaround rather than a fix - a fix would prevent it from being the case, but this, at least, prevents \\*shark from *crashing* if it's the case.",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
